  "summary": "Apiiro finds Claude Code's 'Don't Ask Again' terminal approvals stored raw credentials in local settings, leaking secrets to 1,122 public repos. Hook: 'If you clicked \"Don't Ask Again\" in Claude Code, check your GitHub: over 1,100 repos just leaked active passwords.'",
  "notes": "- Apiiro security researchers discovered thousands of credentials leaked across 1,122 public GitHub repositories\n- Selecting 'Yes, and don't ask again' on terminal command approvals saves the exact raw command into .claude/settings.local.json\n- If commands contained inline database passwords, API tokens, or SSH keys, they were saved in plain text\n- Claude Code's attempt to use global git exclude failed to prevent project-level commits in newly initialized or cloned repos\n- Standard secret scanners missed many tokens embedded in command strings; deleting the file leaves secrets in git history\n- Mitigation: Rotate all terminal-used keys immediately, purge git history with git-filter-repo, add .claude/ to .gitignore",
  "actions": [
   "Created video idea 2026-11-08-claude-code-secret-leak-warning"
  ],
